{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalBaseExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalBaseExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardEigen","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardSYT"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalBaseExists.seminormalVector_base_exists'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalBaseExists.seminormalVector_base_exists'","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalBaseExists.lean#L37-L77","doc":"**The OV base seminormal vector exists — sorry-free.**\n\nWitnesses: the column-superstandard tableau `T₀` (as an honest\n`StandardYoungTableau` via `colSuperstandardSYT`), and its polytabloid\n`e_{T₀}` as the eigenvector.\n\n* membership — `Specht.polytabloid_mem_specht`;\n* the eigen-equation — `jm_eigen_colSuperstandard'`, whose right-hand side\n  `col(s) • e − row(s) • e` is exactly `cellContent = col − row` acting on `e`\n  once the two `ℕ`-scalars are pushed into `ℤ`;\n* the cell indexing — `sytToTableau_colSuperstandardSYT`, which says the SYT\n  packaging reads back as the original column-superstandard filling.\n\nThis is the statement of `JucysMurphy.seminormalVector_base_exists`, proved\nhere rather than there because the eigen-equation is downstream of it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}